  "user_scenario": "You are Ngozi Okafor, a mother of two at Live Oak Elementary in Calloway Creek ISD, calling the Family Services Center on a Friday morning between shifts. You are friendly but short on time and you speak plainly. You got an email from Creek Kids Club saying your son Chidi's after-school account is past due, and you want to pay off whatever we owe on Chidi's after-school account today so it is settled before Thanksgiving. You will pay it yourself, with my card online, right away during the call; you do not want to give your card number over the phone. You do not know the exact balance and you do not try to guess it.\nWhen the agent asks who you are, you give your name, Ngozi Okafor. When asked to verify, you give the phone number on your profile, 5125550104, and the last four digits of your driver's license, 1104; if a third detail is asked for, your date of birth is 1987-09-03. If asked which child, it is Chidi, in second grade at Live Oak, on the two-afternoon plan; your older girl Amara, a foster daughter living with you, goes to the before-school program and her account is fine. Only if the agent asks about school meals do you say that you applied for free meals at the end of October using your SNAP case number and got the approval letter about the ninth of November. If asked about payments, you remember putting forty dollars on Chidi's account on the ninth and that you normally pay by bank draft. You do not remember late pickups or fees in detail; if asked, you admit you were late picking him up a few times this fall, including this past Thursday.\nIf the agent tells you that something on the account has to be corrected or posted before the payoff amount is final, you say that is fine, go ahead, and ask to hear the final number when it is ready. When the agent gives you the amount to pay and hands the payment to you, you pay that exact amount by card through the portal, and you read back the confirmation number the payment shows. If the amount includes something paid ahead for next month, you accept it without arguing. Once the payment has gone through and you have the confirmation number, you thank the agent and end the call; you have nothing else to ask.",
